2026-11-07T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2458) 'the rebac edge generator and the tuples it emits across the RFD corpus in rfd/*.exs.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2458  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2458) 'Does a capability that several RFDs can provide ever get recorded as a real choice, with a preferred order and a fallback the planner can use when one provider fails?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2458  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2458) 'The generator already knows how to turn a capability with multiple providers into an alternative set, ordered by commit date, then publish date, then serial, and a planner that backtracks to the next provider when one fails. The idea was tested on one synthetic pair, but no capability in the RFD corpus today actually has two providers recorded, so the beta's own route never exercises the backtracking path it depends on.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2458  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2458) 'Run a research pass over the corpus and its neighbors, from titles and bodies only, to find capabilities with more than one stated provider, fallback, or rejected approach, and record each as a second `provides` edge in preference order.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2458  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2458) '- Treat this as a research task before a code task: read the cone of RFDs named in the issue and their neighbors for stated alternatives, fallbacks, and rejected approaches.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2458  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2458) '- Where two RFDs plausibly provide the same capability, add a second `provides` edge in preference order so the planner's backtracking has a real pair to exercise.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2458  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2458) '- Candidate pairs raised by the issue, unverified until read: Tailscale versus an SSH tunnel for reaching Bao, standalone versus PC VR streaming for headset rendering, WSL libraries versus this Mac as the desktop client, and two RFDs that both claimed the same guest ELF double capability in an early drafting pass.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2458  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2458) '- Until a pair is verified by reading both RFDs in full, no alternative edge should be committed.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2458  1 LINE
